/// \class WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_d
/// \brief Update module registered as "WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate" with
///        the bit Zero Hour uses for the special power interface; it starts
///        asleep.
///
/// Its constructor installs the vtables of the class and its interfaces,
/// clears one flag and puts the module to sleep indefinitely, so it does
/// no work until something wakes it. Its registration adds the bit Zero Hour
/// uses for the special power interface, and its data
/// (WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData) names a special power template
/// and gives a duration, an attribute modifier, a weapon slot to lock and
/// weapon set flags. Together these suggest a special power that switches
/// the object's weapon mode for a time; this page does not confirm the
/// sequence. BFME 1 has the class; Zero Hour does not.
///
/// \see WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData

/// \fn Module *WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate":
///        creates the module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration when an
/// object whose template lists the module is built. The group page
/// describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData
///                    for this module line, shared with every other object
///                    of the template.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate,
///      WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_d
/// \brief Module data for WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate: the special power
///        it answers to and the weapon mode it applies.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData. Its field
/// parse function, WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse,
/// first registers a shared base table and then its own.
///
/// \par Modding
/// The shared base table, read from retail, has \c SpecialPowerTemplate
/// (a special power template looked up by name with
/// INI::parseSpecialPowerTemplate), \c InitiateSound (read by a dedicated
/// parser) and \c StartsPaused (a boolean). Zero Hour's
/// SpecialPowerModuleData table has these three as well, plus
/// \c UpdateModuleStartsAttack and \c ScriptedSpecialPowerOnly. The class's
/// own fields are:
/// - \c Duration, a duration;
/// - \c AttributeModifier, text (INI::parseAsciiString), so the modifier
///   is kept as a name and looked up later;
/// - \c LockWeaponSlot, a weapon slot chosen by name with
///   INI::parseLookupList from a hard-coded list: \c PRIMARY, \c SECONDARY,
///   \c TERTIARY, \c QUATERNARY or \c QUINARY;
/// - \c WeaponSetFlags, read by a dedicated parser this page does not
///   describe.
///
/// \see WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
