///        builds the module data for one module line and parses its INI
///        block.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// It constructs WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData with its defaults,
/// then, when \p ini is not null, parses the block with
/// INI::initFromINIMultiProc and
/// WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse.
///
/// \param ini  The INI reader positioned at the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores,
///         or null when the allocation fails.
/// \see WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      WeaponModeSpecialPowerUpdateModuleData


